~~Form that has fields:~~
*Design:* five steps: 1 account, 2 verify login email, 3 how families reach you, 4 confirm business email (skipped when it's the login email), 5 all set. Fields:
    first name (step 1)
    last name (step 1)
    password (step 1), with the password rules listed under it (at least 8 characters)
        *Decided by the owner 2026-11-09 (ADR-023 d11):* steps 1 and 2 are BladeBook's own pages, not Cognito's hosted
        sign-up page, so sign-up stays one flow. The browser sends the email, password and code straight to Cognito,
        which creates the account, sends the code and enforces the password rules; BladeBook's servers never see them.
    <!-- business EIN / tbd Canada's version -->
    login email (step 1): private; the coach logs in with it and gets the daily report and the morning email there.
                    Step 2 verifies it with a 6-digit emailed code, with Resend code and Change email links.
    business email ~~(optional and will be login email if left blank)~~ *(step 3: "Use my login email" or "Use a different email". A different address gets a confirmation link, not a code, on step 4, with Resend link, Change address and "Use my login email instead". Families can't reach the coach until it's confirmed.)*
                    (will be what a client responds to if they click reply within an automated email)
    phone number (step 3, optional)
    ~~Display phone number to clients (y/n) checkbox~~ *Design: not at sign-up; it's the Phone number switch on the profile's Visibility tab (C_Coach Profile.md).*
    timezone (step 3)
    currency (step 3): USD or CAD, chosen once. Every lesson is priced in it.

    Profile photo upload (optional, capped at 2MB and resize server-side to 512px)
                         *Profile photo is Phase 2 (ADR-016 d5); MVP shows initials.*
                         (will only be shown once the client enters the coachCode in the client sign up page.)

    paymentInstructions (step 3, "How families pay you")
    ~~Display payment types to clients checkbox~~       : checking this box will show 
                                                        the supplied payment handles in the payment reminder emails
                    *Design: not at sign-up; it's the Payment handles switch on the profile's Visibility tab.*
                    *Replaced 2026-10-12 (ADR-016 d7):* each payment type has its own switch, below.
    PaymentTypes to be included in payment reminder email to client
    Cashapp: (optional)
    Venmo: (optional)
    Paypal: (optional)
    Cash: an "I accept cash" switch.
    *Decided 2026-10-12 (ADR-016 d7):* Cash, Cash App, Venmo and PayPal each get an on/off switch here and on the
        profile. A type switched on is a how-paid option and is shown to approved families. Cash App, Venmo and
        PayPal need their handle to be switched on.
    *Decided 2026-10-12:* Cash comes back as an "I accept cash" switch (`acceptsCash`), at sign-up and on the profile.
        When it's on, Cash is one of the how-paid options. (ADR-016 d7, ADR-003 d4)
    *Decided by the owner 2026-11-12:* a warning sits above the step 3 button ("Save and continue" / "Finish setup"):
        "Check your handles before you save. BladeBook doesn't verify payment handles and isn't responsible for
        payments sent to an incorrect one." It shows whether or not any type is switched on. The profile's Payments
        tab has the same warning (see C_Coach Profile.md).

    Step 5, all set: where families will reach the coach, the coach code with a Copy button, and "Build your teaching
    week" (opens the weekly schedule editor) or "go to your dashboard".

Business email (from ADR-016, moved 2026-11-08):
  *Decided by the owner 2026-10-13 through the Harbor design (design/harbor/coach, sign-up step 4 and Profile → Business
    email):* a business email that differs from the login email must be confirmed by a link before it is used.
  At sign-up, step 3 offers "Use my login email" or "Use a different email". A different address gets a link on
    step 4, with "Resend link", "Change address" and "Use my login email instead".
    *(from ADR-016, amendment 2026-10-13)*
  *Decided by the owner 2026-11-06, settling a conflict with the Harbor design (design/harbor/coach/app.js, sign-up
    step 4):* at sign-up, families can't reach the coach until a different business email is confirmed. Until the link
    is clicked, the login email is not used as the address families reply to. Step 4's banner stands as drawn:
    "Families can't reach you until this is confirmed." A coach who picks "Use my login email" (or "Use my login
    email instead") is reachable straight away.
  What it blocks (owner, same day): the coach code doesn't work until the address is confirmed. No family can sign up
    with, or add, this coach before then. A family who tries sees the ordinary "That code doesn't match a coach"
    message, which reveals nothing about an unfinished sign-up.
  The coach is told: until it's confirmed, the coach's code is shown with "Your code starts working once you confirm
    your business email." Drawn 2026-11-06 in design/harbor/coach/ (today-code-pending,
    profile-details-code-pending, and the code card on signup-4-confirm-email).
    *(from ADR-016, amendment 2026-11-06)*

Not at sign-up:
  *Decided by the owner 2026-11-06, settling a conflict with the Harbor design:* "Text me when a family cancels late"
    is on the profile only (Profile → Visibility & texts), not on the sign-up form. One less question at sign-up.
    *(from ADR-016, amendment 2026-11-06, moved 2026-11-08)*

